knowledge_statements.statement_latex:
For a local first-order oracle returning vectors \(g_0,g_1,\ldots\), call an algorithm span-restricted when
\[
x_{t+1}-x_0\in\operatorname{span}\{g_0,\ldots,g_t\}
\]
for every \(t\). The restriction fails for any admissible algorithm that, for some transcript, selects \(x_{t+1}=x_0+v_t\) with \(v_t\notin\operatorname{span}\{g_0,
\ldots,g_t\}\). A resisting-oracle lower bound whose induction uses span membership therefore applies only to the span-restricted class unless an additional resisting construction proves that leaving the span cannot improve the worst-case guarantee.
